    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1014">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1032"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Señor du Bosc to Mr. Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain at Washington</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                17, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Day</hi>: Through the minister of foreign
                    affairs in Madrid I have been instructed by Her Majesty the Queen Regent of
                    Spain, my august sovereign, to convey to the President of the United States of
                    America her expression of grief at the misfortune which has befallen the
                    American Navy in Spanish waters. Deferring entirely to your judgment in the
                    matter, I would suggest that it would be fit and proper that I should obey Her
                    Majesty’s instructions in person, and not simply <pb facs="1129" n="1033"
                        xml:id="pg1033"/> in an official communication. If you agree with me upon
                    this point, I beg you to ask the President to grant me an audience for that
                    express purpose. Shall be glad to hear your views on the matter.</p>
                <p>Believe me, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan du Bosc</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
